      "spam": false,
      "value": "There are quite a few VR games that handle inventory and special interaction to objects through special objects being held (like lockpicks) that are accessed through interacting with a certain trigger area on the player's model in order to free up controller button space. Being able to place \"interactive bubbles\" with some selections as to what they do - toggle animation, toggle active object, toggle sound, etc - would make VR work a whole lot more immersive and fun (as well as educational).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
